<decision #track.integrate_holon_task_workflows_end_to_end.file_xnl_issuer apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?>What is the organization snapshot authority for the local-file product journey?</?>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?>Issue it from the real pure File-XNL capsule before ResourcePackage admission; never hand-build or read it from SQLite.</?>
    <decision-text ?>P1 writes the organization through `holarchy-file-xnl-capsule@0.2.0`, reconstructs that file authority, and admits its canonical snapshot bytes plus issuance receipt into the ResourcePackage. Workflow execution consumes only the admitted immutable material. Live authority changes are visible only through explicit organization replan.</?>
    <rationale ?>This closes Mission Replan 004: the product E2E must exercise the actual local-file owner and issuer while preserving Definition→Instance→Run freeze and keeping database migration outside the runtime closure.</?>
    <evidence ?>Completed Track `separate-file-xnl-runtime-capsule-and-snapshot-port`; npm releases `holarchy-core-logic@0.1.2`, `holarchy-file-xnl-logic@0.1.1`, `holarchy-file-xnl-support@0.1.1`, `holarchy-file-xnl-capsule@0.2.0`.</?>
  )>
  <confidence ?>high</?>
  <reversibility ?>moderate</?>
)>
